<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Humphrey IV of Toron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1166–1198</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Humphrey IV of Toron was a baron of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>, stepson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raynald-of-chatillon">Raynald of Châtillon</a> and heir of Toron and Oultrejordain. He married Isabella, half-sister of King Baldwin IV, in 1183, but in 1186 refused to be crowned by the barons opposed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a> and submitted to Guy and Sibylla. In 1190 the marriage was annulled so that Isabella could marry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat">Conrad of Montferrat</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/humphrey-iv-of-toron.jpg" alt="Humphrey IV of Toron" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author from northern France · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Humphrey_IV_of_Toron_Isabela.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
